      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "El tercer día, Set no esperó su turno.",
          "en": "On the third day, Set did not wait his turn."
        },
        {
          "es": "Se abrió paso por su cuenta, rompiendo el costado de su madre para salir antes de tiempo.",
          "en": "He forced his own way out, tearing through his mother's side to be born before his time."
        },
        {
          "es": "Tenía la piel clara y el pelo rojo como el desierto, y la fuerza de una tormenta.",
          "en": "He had pale skin, hair as red as the desert, and the strength of a storm."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los egipcios lo veneraban y le tenían miedo: era el señor del desierto, del trueno y de las tormentas de arena.",
          "en": "The Egyptians worshipped him and feared him: he was lord of the desert, of thunder and of sandstorms."
        },
        {
          "es": "Era tan fuerte que, más adelante, el mismo Ra lo pondría en la proa de su barca para defenderla en la noche.",
          "en": "He was so strong that later Ra himself would place him at the prow of his boat to defend it through the night."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los egipcios creían que esos cinco días eran peligrosos, y el tercero, el de Set, el peor de todos.",
          "en": "The Egyptians believed those five days were dangerous, and the third, Set's day, the worst of all."
        }
      ],
